# Line endings: LF in the repository AND in every checkout, whatever core.autocrlf says.
#
# Git for Windows installs with core.autocrlf=true, which checks text files out with CRLF.
# The shared contract vectors and the tic-tac-toe template cases are copied verbatim from
# ikigai-core and ikigai-tutorial, and devtools `vector-drift` compares them by their raw
# bytes, so a CRLF checkout reads as drift. `eol=lf` on a path overrides core.autocrlf for
# it. The index is already LF throughout (`git ls-files --eol`, 2026-10-11), so this needs
# no renormalize. Ledger #1205.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Named explicitly, so content detection can never decide them.
tests/vectors/*.json          text eol=lf
tests/ttt_template_cases.txt  text eol=lf
*.py                          text eol=lf
*.sh                          text eol=lf
